"Create a Secure MCP Tunnel in OpenAI Platform and replace <TUNNEL_ID> in the setup command below." = "Open the Tunnels management page below, choose Create tunnel, and create a tunnel. Copy the ID shown after creation; it starts with tunnel_. Do not invent this value or use the API key here.";
"Set CONTROL_PLANE_API_KEY in Terminal, then run the Tunnel setup command. Never enter the API key in FolderSync." = "Create or use a runtime API key from the API keys page below. In Terminal, set CONTROL_PLANE_API_KEY to that key. Do not use an organization admin key, and never paste the key into FolderSync or ChatGPT.";
"Run the Tunnel command below and keep tunnel-client running while ChatGPT scans or calls the tools." = "Replace <TUNNEL_ID> in the setup command with the copied tunnel_… ID, then run it once. Run the doctor command to check the profile, then run the Tunnel command and keep that Terminal window open while ChatGPT uses FolderSync.";
"In ChatGPT's developer-mode app registration screen, choose Connection → Tunnel instead of Server URL, select the same Tunnel, and scan the tools." = "In ChatGPT on the web, open the developer-mode custom app creation screen. Choose Connection → Tunnel instead of Server URL, select the same Tunnel, scan the tools, and create or enable the app. A workspace admin may need to enable developer mode or approve it.";
"Before asking ChatGPT to work, select the FolderSync sync list you want to use. MCP can read and change files only inside that list's local folder; a GitHub endpoint is synchronized through the selected local folder." = "Before asking ChatGPT to work, select the FolderSync sync list you want to use. MCP can read and change files only inside that list's local folder. For GitHub edits that must arrive locally, configure the direction as GitHub → local.";
"When ChatGPT finishes editing GitHub, ask it to call finalize_github_sync as the last step. Set the sync direction to GitHub → local so the completed source is pulled into the selected folder." = "When ChatGPT finishes editing GitHub, ask it to call finalize_github_sync as the last step. This pulls the completed GitHub source into the selected local folder. If the Mac is off or tunnel-client is stopped, run the command after reconnecting.";
